Wildfire management-task force and state 25LSO-0663, 1.0
forester.
FISCAL NOTE
This bill contains an appropriation of $1,000,000 from the GENERAL FUND for the
Special Contingency Division of the Governor’s Office, unit 0601. This
appropriation is effective immediately.
This bill contains an appropriation of $1,263,966 from the GENERAL FUND for the
Disaster Contingency Unit in the Homeland Security Division of the Governor’s
Office, unit 1106. This appropriation is effective immediately.
This bill contains an appropriation of $20,000,000 from the GENERAL FUND to the
Emergency Fire Suppression Account in the Office of State Lands and Investments
(OSLI). This appropriation is effective immediately.
This bill contains an appropriation of up to $20,000,000 from the GENERAL FUND to
be deposited by the State Auditor in the Legislative Stabilization Reserve
Account (LSRA) for repayment of funds borrowed on or before June 30, 2025 under
2024 Wyoming Session Laws, Ch. 118, sec. 301(b). This appropriation is effective
immediately.
For the period beginning July 1, 2025 and ending June 30, 2026, the Governor is
authorized to borrow from the LSRA up to $30,000,000 to fight wildfires in the
event reserves in the OSLI’s Forestry Division have been exhausted.
This bill repeals 2024 Session Laws, Ch. 118, sec. 301(b).
This bill contains an appropriation of $25,000 from the GENERAL FUND to the
Legislative Service Office (LSO). This appropriation is effective immediately.
This bill contains an appropriation of $25,000 from the GENERAL FUND to the
Governor's Office. This appropriation is effective immediately.
DETAIL OF APPROPRIATION
Agency #: 201 Agency Name: Legislative Service Office
Unit: 0101 Administration
EXPENDITURE BY SERIES AND YEAR FY 2025 FY 2026 FY 2027
0100 Personnel/Benefit Costs $1,400 $5,500 $1,400
0200 Supportive Services Costs $2,600 $10,200 $2,600
Total Expenditure Per Year: $4,000 $15,700 $4,000
Grand Total Expenditure: $23,700
Total Appropriated to Agency: $25,000
Total Appropriated by Fund:
GENERAL FUND $25,000
Description of appropriation:
The $25,000 appropriation to the LSO will be expended for the payment of salary,
per diem and mileage expenses for the four legislators appointed to the task
force. The above estimate assumes meeting days in FY 2025, FY 2026 and FY 2027.
